# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution): at 188 rad/s (300 mm/s) something fails; hv0.sim_dist,
# zeroed then, is how far the axis went (1 rad = 1.59 mm). Coasting takes
# ~16 rad (26 mm) and ~180 ms.
# estop_f4dead.test without the flag (hv0.brake_on_loss = 0, as an F4
# older than this): the F3 switches off on its timeout, the axis coasts.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
hv0.sim_vel
hv0.sim_dist = 0
hv0.brake_on_loss = 0
run 0.001
hv0.sim_f4_dead = 1
run 0.3
hv0.sim_dist
hv0.sim_f3_brake
@expect hv0.sim_dist > 14
@expect hv0.sim_f3_brake == 0
